      "text": "This problem can be solved by subtracting from 1 the chance that all four sides match. For simplicity, the following probability calculation is not arbitrary.\n\n1. The probability that all dice matching is denoted by ${1 \\over 6}$ since a six-sided die has 6 equally likely possibilities.\n2. All dice matching is calculated independently of one another because each roll is independent of the others.\n3. Therefore, the chance that all four dice match is calculated as ${1 \\over 6}$ multiplied by itself four times, which simplifies to ${1 \\over 6} \\times {1 \\over 6} \\times {1 \\over 6} \\times {1 \\over 6} = {1 \\over 1296}$.\n4. The result of 1 minus the probability that all dice match gives us 1 - ${1 \\over 1296}$, which is the probability that not all the dice match.\n5. Solving this mathematical expression gives ${1 \\over 1295}$.\n\nThe result, rounded, is the probability that not all dice match, which is:\n$\\boxed{\\frac{1}{1295}}$.",
